\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\rem ESFM v0.6 JDE
\rem WORDTABLE OET-LV_NT_word_table.tsv
\h Yehudah
\toc1 Yehudah (Jude)
\toc2 Yehudah
\toc3 Jud.
\mt1 Yehudah (Jude)
\is1 Introduction
\is2 Author
\ip This letter was written by Yehudah the younger brother of Ya’akov. (Note that he wasn’t the Yudas who handed Yeshua over to the Jewish religious leaders. Note also that Yudas is mistakenly called Yude in most English Bibles, and Yacob is quite wrongly called James in most English Bibles.)
\is2 This letter
\ip We don’t know which group of believers that this letter was sent to. Here in this letter, Yehudah warns the believers about teachers of false doctrines who teach that it’s okay for believers to continue sinning since they’ll just be forgiven due to God’s mercy. That’s the reason Yehudah wrote this, to warn the believers so that they won’t fall for false beliefs, but instead will continue to follow the true teaching that came from God. He also encourages the readers that it’s necessary to strive to continue in their faith in God along with turning away from evil actions.
\iot Main components of Yehudah’ letter
\io1 Introduction \ior 1-2\ior*
\io1 The work and judgement of false teachers \ior 3-16\ior*
\io1 Warnings and teaching \ior 17-23\ior*
\io1 The need to honour god \ior 24-25\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\rem NOTE: This USFM file was exported from the ESFM source file with some loss of features, so don’t edit this derived file.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \add This letter is from\add* Yehudah \add (Jude; Grk. Yudas)\add*, a slave \nd of Yeshua \+add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\+add* the messiah\nd*, and brother of Ya’akov \add (James; Grk. Yakobos)\add*.\x + \xo 1: \xt Mat 13:55; Mrk 6:3.\x* It’s written to all those who have been called and loved by \nd God\nd* the father and who have kept \add believing\add* \nd in Yeshua the messiah\nd*.
\p
\v 2 \add I pray\add* that you all will experience \add God’s\add* mercy and peace, and a bountiful supply of love.
\s1 The judgement of false-teachers and god-rejecters
\p
\v 3 Friends, I was so enthusiastic to write to you concerning our salvation that we have in common, but I needed to write to you all, encouraging you to stand strong for the teaching that was entrusted to the believers at a certain point in time.
\v 4 Because some people have quietly come into \add our groups\add* who think they can \add take advantage of\add* \nd God’s\nd* grace to bring in immoral lifestyles and disowning the only master, and our boss who’s \nd Yeshua \+add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\+add* the messiah\nd*. But they are destined for judgement.
\p
\v 5 Now I want to remind you that although you all know how \nd Yeshua\nd* rescued our people out of Mitsrayim \add (Egypt)\add*,\x + \xo 5: \xt Exo 12:51.\x* yet \add at the same time\add* he destroyed the ones who didn’t believe.\x + \xo 5: \xt Num 14:29-30.\x*
\v 6 Even the messengers who broke their own \add rules\add* and left their own domain have been held in eternal chains in the darkness until the time of judgement in the great day.\x + \xo 1:6: \xt 2Pe 2:4.\x*
\v 7 Similarly Sedom and Amorah \add (Gomorrah)\add* and the towns around them stay in our minds as an example of the judgement of eternal fire due to similar sexual perversions.\x + \xo 7: \xt Gen 19:1-24.\x*
\p
\v 8 in the same way these dreamers defile \add their\add* own bodies while rejecting authority and dishonouring those who should be honoured.
\v 9 Even Mika’el \add (Michael)\add*, \add one of\add* the top messengers,\x + \xo 9: \xt Dan 10:13,21; 12:1; Rev 12:7.\x* when he was arguing with the devil about Mosheh’s \add (Moses)\add* body,\x + \xo 9: \xt Deu 34:6.\x* he didn’t belittle him, but left it to \nd Yahweh\nd* to punish \add him\add*.\x + \xo 9: \xt Zech 3:2.\x*
\v 10 But these people mock what they don’t even grasp, but they’ll be destroyed by what their animal instincts do understand.
\v 11 Oh dear! Because they’ve followed the actions of Kayin \add (Cain)\add*\x + \xo 11: \xt Gen 4:3-8; 1Yhn 3:12.\x* and have embraced the deception of Bil’am \add (Balaam)\add* for monetary gain,\x + \xo 11: \xt Num 22–24; 31:16; 2Pe 2:15-16.\x* so too they’ll perish like Korah’s destruction.\x + \xo 11: \xt Num 16:1-35.\x*
\v 12 These are the people who ruin your love feasts when they eat without shame and only \add look after\add* themselves. They’re like clouds that are blown away by the \add wind\add* without bringing the needed rain or trees that don’t produce any fruit then are doubly useless by falling over;
\v 13 like wild waves in the ocean that foam in their own shame or like \add unreliable\add* wandering stars that are already doomed to the darkest darkness in the next age.
\p
\v 14 Hanok \add (Enoch)\add* (the seventh generation from Adam)\x + \xo 14: \xt Gen 5:18,21-24.\x* prophesied \add way back then\add* about these people, “Look, \nd Yahweh\nd*, surrounded by tens of thousands of his holy \add messengers\add*, came
\v 15 to sentence everybody and to punish everyone who rejected God for everything they did that demonstrated this rejection and everything they said against him.”
\v 16 This includes \add their\add* grumbling and complaining, the fulfilling of their own lustful desires, the arrogant way that they spoke, and their flattering of others in order to gain from them.
\s1 Keep your faith and keep ministering to others
\p
\v 17 But you, friends, always be thinking about how the missionaries of our \nd master Yeshua \+add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\+add* the messiah\nd*
\v 18 told you that mockers near the end of time would come out following their own god-rejecting lusts.\x + \xo 18: \xt 2Pe 3:3.\x*
\v 19 These people will cause division as they just demonstrate sensuality since they don’t know \add God’s\add* \nd spirit\nd*.
\v 20 But you, friends, work to increase your faith in God, praying as \nd the\nd* holy \nd spirit\nd* helps you.
\v 21 Keep receiving \nd God’s\nd* love as you look forward to \add living\add* forever thanks to the mercy of our \nd master\nd*, \nd Yeshua the messiah\nd*.
\p
\v 22 Show grace to those \add still\add* doubting
\v 23 whereas others need to be ‘snatched out of the fire’ in order to be saved. To some, show mercy but very carefully, hating even their clothes which reflect their crude lifestyles.
\s1 Honouring God
\p
\v 24-25 Our \nd master\nd*, Yeshua \add (Jesus; Grk. Yesus)\add* \nd the messiah\nd*, is the infallible \nd one\nd* who is quite capable of \add looking after\add* all of \add us\add* so that \add we\add* can stand blameless in front of him and praise him in his full honour and greatness. Let us honour and praise our only \nd God\nd* and saviour, acknowledging \add his\add* greatness and power and authority through Yeshua from before the creation, right through \add these current times\add*, and in the age to come. \add May it be so\add*.
